Dedicated Python scripts (e.g. \texttt{performance\_test\_dot\_thread\_multi.py}) were developed to automate the execution of multi-threaded PQC-DNS queries. Each session consisted of 100 parallel DNS queries using Python's \texttt{ThreadPoolExecutor}. Key logic that differ from \texttt{performance\_test\_dot.py} is \textbf{Function \texttt{run\_session(session\_id)}}. This function performs a single benchmarking session by concurrently issuing multiple DNS queries using a thread pool. It measures network usage and latency as follows:

\begin{verbatim}
Function run_session(session_id):
    net_before := get total bytes sent/received
    start_time := current time

    Launch thread pool with 100 workers:
        For each worker:
            Submit run_dns_query() to executor

    Wait for all threads to complete

    end_time := current time
    net_after := get total bytes sent/received

    latency_ms := (end_time - start_time) * 1000
    bandwidth_kb := (net_after - net_before) / 1024

    Write metrics to session-level CSV
\end{verbatim}
