\section{Bound of $\eta_T$ without Assumption 1}\label{sec:appendixB}
We treat here the particular situation where Assumption \ref{ass: 1} might not hold. This case
%, illustrated in Figure \ref{fig:not working cas assumption}, 
might occur for a particular cut near a very acute angle of the interface. We are interested in the changes incurred to Lemma \ref{lem: bound_3_effica} and Theorem \ref{thm: efficiency_IRT}. Then for $T\in \T^{\Gamma}$, we can still construct one (instead of two) regular shaped triangle $T^*$ such that $\Gamma_T$ is one of its edges and $T^*$ is contained in one of the subdomains, let's say $\Omega^*$. 

%\begin{figure}[ht!]
%    \centering
%    \includegraphics[width=0.25\linewidth]{Article 2-1/figures/assumption_not.png}
%    \caption{Particular mesh/interface geometry where Assumption 1 is not valid}
%    \label{fig:not working cas assumption}
%\end{figure}

We then have, in the proof of Lemma \ref{lem: bound_3_effica}, 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
\|[K\nabla u_h\cdot n_{\Gamma}]\|_{\Gamma_T}^2 & \lesssim \bigg|\int_{\Gamma_T}[K\nabla u_h\cdot n_\Gamma]\psi_\Gamma\ds \bigg|\\
& = \frac{1}{\bar\omega_*}\bigg|\int_{\Gamma_T}(k_*\nabla (u_{h,*}-u)\cdot n_\Gamma-\{K\nabla (u_h- u)\cdot n_\Gamma\})\psi_\Gamma\ds\bigg|,
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
where $\bar{\omega}_*:=1-\omega_*$ and where we have used that $\bar{\omega}_i[w]=(-1)^{i+1}(w_i-\{w\})$ with $w_i=k_i\nabla u_{h,i}\cdot n_{\Gamma}$, $i=1, 2$.

Then we apply the triangle inequality and bound the first term exactly as in the proof of Lemma \ref{lem: bound_3_effica}, by integrating by parts on $T^*$. The second term is bounded by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, combined with the trace inequality for $\psi_{\Gamma}$ on $\Gamma_T\subset \partial T^*$. 

We thus obtain, instead of the estimate of Lemma \ref{lem: bound_3_effica}, the following bound: 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
h_T^{1/2}\|[K\nabla u_h\cdot n_{\Gamma}]\|_{\Gamma_T}\lesssim &\frac{1}{\bar\omega_*} \bigg( \frac{k_*^{1/2}h_T^{1/2}}{|\Gamma_T|^{1/2}} \nrmL[T^*]{k_*^{1/2}\nabla (u_{h,*}- u)}+ h_T \nrmL[T^*]{f-f_h} \\
&+ k_*^{1/2}j_{*,\Delta_T}(u_{h,*},u_{h,*})^{1/2}+ h_T^{1/2}\nrmL[\Gamma_T]{\{K\nabla (u- u_h)\cdot n_\Gamma\}}\bigg).
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
This leads to two changes in Theorem \ref{thm: efficiency_IRT}: one concerns the efficiency constant which now becomes, using $k_*/\bar{\omega}_*=k_1+k_2\le 2k_{max}  $ and  $1/\bar{\omega}_i\le k_{max}/k_{min}$ :
$ C'_{T}= C_{T}\sqrt{k_{max}}/\sqrt{k_{min}}$, and the other concerns the norm of the local error, which is now: 
$$\||u-u_h|\|_{h,\Delta_T}^2:=\|u-u_h\|_{h,\Delta_T}^2+\sum_{T\in \mathcal{T}_h^{\Gamma}\cap \Delta_T}\frac{h_T}{k_{\Gamma}} \nrmL[\Gamma_T]{\{K\nabla (u- u_h)\cdot n_\Gamma\}}^2.$$

