\subsection*{Structure of the paper} In Section \ref{sec:2}, we present some preliminaries on H\"ormander's $L_2$ method, along with a concise discussion of its applications in Brunn--Minkowski theory. In Section \ref{sec:comp}, we use the $L_2$ method to derive a general formula for the second derivative of weighted marginals in terms of solutions to certain elliptic PDE, while in Sections \ref{sec:main} and \ref{sec:log-conc} we combine this formula with spectral estimates to deduce our weighted concavity principles, Theorems \ref{thm:bbl} and \ref{cor:prekopa}. Finally, in Section \ref{sec:poincare}, we use Theorem \ref{thm:bbl} to derive the weighted Poincar\'e-type inequality of Theorem \ref{thm:poincare} and in Section \ref{sec:last} we present some further remarks and open questions that arise from this work.

