\subsection*{Related work} While the present paper was in final stages of preparation, the preprint \cite{AL25} of Aishwarya and Li appeared on arXiv, containing results closely related to Theorem \ref{thm:bbl} in the special case that the rotationally invariant measure $\mu$ is the standard Gaussian.  More specifically, Theorem 1 is \emph{equivalent} to a $\mu$-weighted analogue of the Borell--Brascamp--Lieb inequalities \eqref{eq:bbl1}, \eqref{eq:bbl2} when the even functions $f^\kappa$ and $g^\kappa$ are assumed to be concave on their supports.  In contrast to the local $L_2$ method that we develop here to tackle these problems, the authors of \cite{AL25} use a refreshing information theoretic approach to derive the same conclusion when $f$ and $g$ are assumed to be merely log-concave,  yet only in the special case that $\mu$ is the standard Gaussian measure.

