\subsubsection{Oblique Ionograms Synthesis}
The fourth-stage experiment considered actual HF communication link data to construct synthetic oblique ionograms for the O-wave, comparing them with observed ionograms to validate RTM-GD’s ability to accurately replicate real propagation behavior. We focused on evaluating echo structure morphology and maximum usable frequency (MUF) accuracy. We selected Suzhou–Wuhan and Lanzhou–Wuhan links, conducting simulations at six representative moments. Electron density data was generated using the IRI-2020 model, reconstructed using GD interpolation, and ray trajectories were obtained through joint frequency–elevation scanning. Synthetic ionograms (red squares) were then compared with observational data (blue circles), as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:IonogSyn}.
