  \includegraphics[width=.7\linewidth]{Logit1.png}
  \caption{Logit Lens heatmap showing predicted token probabilities at each layer for a financial prompt}
  \label{fig:Logit}
\end{figure}

Figure \ref{fig:Logit_Diff} shows the average logit difference between the words \textbf{rise} and \textbf{fall} across different layers of the model. The negative logit difference in the earlier layers (0-4) indicates that the model initially prefers \textbf{fall} over \textbf{rise} when processing the input. However, as the model progresses through layers 5 to 10, there is a shift toward a higher preference for \textbf{rise}, particularly in the deeper layers (9-10), where the difference becomes more pronounced. This suggests that the deeper layers are refining the model's judgment, leading to a stronger final decision in favor of \textbf{rise}, showing the model's increased confidence in this choice as it processes the input.


