\begin{quote} \textit{"With recession risk the stock price of company will likely"} \end{quote}

The corresponding heatmap is shown in Figure \ref{fig:Log_Reverse}. As with the previous figure, the X-axis represents the input tokens and the Y-axis represents the model layers. In this case, the model's predictions shift differently, reflecting the more negative context embedded in the prompt. We observe that the model increasingly favors negative outcomes such as "fall" and "decline" as it moves through the layers, indicating that the model adjusts its expectations appropriately in response to recession-related terms. Again, the color intensity reflects the probability assigned to each predicted next word, allowing for visualization of how confident the model becomes at each processing stage. 

