This figure shows the universal lower bound  for the pilot information on another scale, namely relative to  the information $I_{\delta}:={\eta_f^2}/{\delta^2}$ needed for achieving a power of $1-\beta$ at the true or a priori assumed alternative $\vartheta=\delta$ with a single fixed-size sample test: The vertical axis of this figure is
