\keywords{anti-dendriform algebra, quasi-triangular anti-dendriform
 bialgebra, factorizable anti-dendriform bialgebra, relative Rota-Baxter operator}
\begin{document}
\begin{abstract}
We introduce a notion of quasi-triangular anti-dendriform bialgebras, which can be induced by
the solutions of the AD-YBE whose symmetric parts are invariant. A factorizable anti-dendriform bialgebra 
leads to a factorization
of the underlying anti-dendriform algebra. Moreover, relative Rota-Baxter operators with
 weights are introduced to characterize the solutions of the AD-YBE whose symmetric 
 parts are invariant. Finally, we interpret factorizable 
anti-dendriform bialgebras in terms of quadratic Rota-Baxter anti-dendriform algebras.

\end{abstract}

